<title>RUSSIA: LUKoil says U.S. approves its ADRs on prefs.</title>
<headline>LUKoil says U.S. approves its ADRs on prefs.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's biggest oil company OAO Neftyanaya Kompaniya LUKoil  said on Thursday it had received approval from the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to issue level-one American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) on its preferred shares.  </p>
<p>One ADR will correspond to two LUKoil preferred shares, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>LUKoil already has an ADR programme for its ordinary shares. These ADRs are listed in Berlin, Frankfurt and on the NASDAQ bulletin board.</p>
<p>LUKoil has 65.01 million preferred shares, amounting to 9.10 percent of its capital.</p>
<p>At 0945 GMT LUKoil preferred shares were last traded at $12.49 after closing at $11.75 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ordinaries were $15.30 after $15.10.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
